# UI Studio Onboard — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and populate the variables needed for your onboarding mode.
# NEVER commit .env to version control. This file (.env.example) is safe to commit.
# NEVER put actual token values in active-brand.json — store env var NAMES only.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GITHUB ACCESS (Developer persona — git/GitHub extraction)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Personal Access Token for GitHub API and git clone access.
# Required for: token file extraction, component source scanning, repo refresh.
# Scopes needed: repo (for private repos) or public_repo (for public repos).
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NPM / PRIVATE REGISTRY ACCESS (Enterprise persona)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auth token for npm or private registry access.
# Required for: extracting design tokens and component inventory from npm packages.
# For Verdaccio or other private registries, this is typically a base64-encoded credential.
NPM_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GIT TOKEN (Developer persona — non-GitHub git servers)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Auth token for git clone/pull from non-GitHub git servers (GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure DevOps).
# Required when: token or component repository is hosted outside GitHub.
GIT_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STORYBOOK ACCESS (Designer/Developer persona — Storybook component inventory)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Authorization header value for protected Storybook deployments.
# Format: "Bearer <token>" or "Basic <base64-credential>"
# Required only if the Storybook URL is behind authentication.
# The env var NAME (not this value) is stored in repository.storybook.auth_header_env_var.
STORYBOOK_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Figma MCP connection:
#   Figma access is handled through the connected Figma MCP account — no token needed here.
#   The connected account must have at least "can view" access to the design system file.
#   If access fails during Phase 0 verification, share the file with the connected account.
#
# Supernova MCP connection:
#   Supernova access is handled through the Supernova MCP connection — no token needed here.
#   The workspace ID is stored in repository.supernova_workspace in the config.
#
# .npmrc generation for enterprise registries:
#   setup.py will generate a temporary .npmrc file at extraction time using NPM_TOKEN.
#   The file is deleted after extraction completes.
#   If the registry requires a custom scope or URL, set registry_url and scope
#   in the repository.npm block of the config.
